  "title": "First words",
  "goal": "Greet people politely, say yes and no, thank, apologise and take your leave in Telugu.",
  "intro": "Telugu greetings are warm and a little formal. The all-purpose greeting is *నమస్కారం* (namaskāram), said with palms joined. Politeness is carried by the little word *అండి* (aṇḍi), which you can add to almost anything to make it respectful: *సరే అండి* (okay, sir/madam).\n\nTelugu also has a charming way of saying goodbye: you don't say 'I'm going', you say *వెళ్ళొస్తాను* (veḷḷostānu), 'I'll go and come back'.",
